---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Written 2026-07-28 from the actual implementation, corrected 2026-08-02
// (legal self-review): GA4 (G-65PEMEYW2M) loads ONLY after Accept on the
// consent banner (Consent.astro). Sign-in (register confirm, Google, magic
// link) sets ONE strictly necessary session cookie, smg_s, 90 days, HttpOnly;
// the old copy denied it existed and that was false. Consent choice and site
// preferences live in localStorage, which DOES leave the device when the user
// asks (Email list via /api/backup, account sync via /api/sync); the old
// "never sent to anyone" line was false too. Service worker caches pages.
const UPDATED = '2 August 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Cookie Policy | Save My Gig"
  description="The one optional analytics cookie Save My Gig uses, the sign-in cookie, what lives in your browser instead of cookies, and how to refuse or remove all of it."
  path="/legal/cookies"
  noindex
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">LEGAL</div>
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">Last updated: {UPDATED} · Part of <a href="/legal">the legal shelf</a></p>

    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">
      Short version: this site sets no cookies until you accept analytics on
      the banner or sign in to an account. Signing in sets one strictly
      necessary cookie that keeps you signed in, nothing else. Analytics is
      optional and off by default. Decline and the site works exactly the same.
    </p>

    <div class="panel">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">The one category of cookies we use</h2>
      <p class="dim">
        <strong>Analytics (optional, off by default).</strong> If you accept on
        the banner, we load Google Analytics 4 (Google LLC), which sets cookies
        beginning with <span class="mono">_ga</span>. We use it to see which
        pages actually help DJs and where people get stuck, nothing more. If you
        decline, Google Analytics is never loaded and these cookies are never
        set. Google describes its own processing in its privacy policy at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        We set <strong>no advertising cookies</strong> and do
        <strong>no cross-site tracking</strong>, with or without consent.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">The sign-in cookie (strictly necessary)</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        If you register or sign in, we set one cookie named
        <span class="mono">smg_s</span>. It is what keeps this device signed
        in. It holds a signed session token, not a tracking ID, lasts 90 days,
        and is never used for analytics or advertising. Signing out or deleting
        your account removes it. Never sign in and this cookie is never set.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">What lives in your browser instead</h3>
      <p class="dim">
        The site stores some data in your browser's local storage. Local storage
        is not a cookie and never travels with your requests on its own. It
        stays on your device unless you ask us to move it: the Email list
        button sends your list to your inbox through Brevo, and account sync
        stores a copy on our servers so your other devices can load it. Both
        are described in the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. It
        holds your cookie choice itself (so the banner does not ask on every
        visit), your checklist (items, edits, ticks, notes), your registration
        on this device, including the email address and name you registered
        with, and a few small preferences such as dismissed notices.
      </p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        The site can also install a small offline cache (a service worker) so
        the rescue pages keep working in a basement booth with no signal. That
        cache contains our pages, nothing about you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Changing your mind</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        Clear this site's cookies in your browser and the banner asks again on
        your next visit. Careful with the nuclear option: clearing all site
        data also deletes your checklist from this device, so download or email
        your list first. You can also block cookies for this site entirely in
        your browser settings; the rescue flow does not need them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="dim" style="font-size:0.85rem;margin-top:2rem">
      This policy is part of <a href="/legal">the legal shelf</a>, alongside the
      <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. Questions:
      <a href="mailto:info@savemygig.com">info@savemygig.com</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
